      "numbered_text": "1: ---\n2: title: Vercel Hobby Plan\n3: product: vercel\n4: url: /docs/plans/hobby\n5: canonical_url: \"https://vercel.com/docs/plans/hobby\"\n6: last_updated: 2026-11-12\n7: type: reference\n8: prerequisites:\n9: - /docs/plans\n10: related:\n11: - /docs/pricing/taxes\n12: - /docs/global-config/using-global-config\n13: - /docs/pricing/regional-pricing\n14: - /docs/functions/usage-and-pricing\n15: - /docs/image-optimization/limits-and-pricing\n16: summary: Learn about the Hobby plan and how it compares to the Pro plan.\n17: install_vercel_plugin: npx plugins add vercel/vercel-plugin\n18: search_with_vercel_cli: npx vercel@latest docs search \"<query>\"\n19: ---\n20: # Vercel Hobby Plan\n21: The Hobby plan is **free** and includes a generous set of features on a **per month** basis:\n22: <!-- docsgraph:related -->\n23: ## Related pages\n24: > **For AI agents:** Follow these links to understand how this page connects to the rest of the Vercel ecosystem. For the full cross-link map (inbound, outbound, prerequisites, and semantic neighbors), see the .graph.md link below.\n25: - [Agent Runs](https://eve.dev/docs/observability/agent-runs) — Inspect eve sessions in Vercel and configure the Agent Runs destination.\n26: - [The Complete Guide to Vercel Daemons](https://vercel.com/kb/guide/vercel-daemons) — Run background workers with Vercel Daemons. Learn how to deploy container images, configure resources, handle shutdowns,\n27: - [Pricing on Vercel](https://vercel.com/docs/pricing) — Learn about Vercel's pricing model, including the resources and services that are billed, and how they are priced.\n28: - [Billing FAQ for Pro Plan](https://vercel.com/docs/plans/pro-plan/billing) — This page covers frequently asked questions around payments, invoices, and billing on the Pro plan.\n29: - [Manage and optimize usage](https://vercel.com/docs/pricing/manage-and-optimize-usage) — Understand how to manage and optimize your usage on Vercel, learn how to track your usage, set up alerts, and optimize y\n30: - [Fair Use Guidelines](https://vercel.com/docs/limits/fair-use-guidelines) — Learn how Vercel applies fair use guidelines across plans and usage-based resources.\n31: - [Observability Plus](https://vercel.com/docs/observability/observability-plus) — Learn about using Observability Plus and its limits.\n32: Full cross-link map for this page: [/docs/plans/hobby.graph.md](/docs/plans/hobby.graph.md)\n33: <!-- /docsgraph:related -->\n34: > **💡 Note:** All prices shown are in USD and exclude value-added tax (VAT), goods and services tax (GST), and other applicable taxes. Taxes are calculated based on your billing address and added to your invoice where required by law. [Learn more about taxes](/docs/pricing/taxes).\n35: | Resource | Hobby Included Usage |\n36: | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------- |\n37: | [Global Config Reads](/docs/global-config/using-global-config#reading-data-from-global-configs) | First 100,000 |\n38: | [Global Config Writes](/docs/global-config/using-global-config#writing-data-to-global-configs) | First 100 |\n39: | [Fast Data Transfer](/docs/pricing/regional-pricing) | First 100 GB |\n40: | [Fast Origin Transfer](/docs/pricing/regional-pricing) | First 10 GB |\n41: | [CDN Requests](/docs/pricing/regional-pricing) | First 1,000,000 |\n42: | [Active CPU](/docs/functions/usage-and-pricing) | 4 CPU-hrs |\n43: | [Provisioned Memory](/docs/functions/usage-and-pricing) | 360 GB-hrs |\n44: | [Function Invocations](/docs/functions/usage-and-pricing) | First 1,000,000 |\n45: | [Image Transformations](/docs/image-optimization/limits-and-pricing#image-transformations) | First 5,000 |\n46: | [Image Cache Reads](/docs/image-optimization/limits-and-pricing#image-cache-reads) | First 300,000 |\n47: | [Image Cache Writes](/docs/image-optimization/limits-and-pricing#image-cache-writes) | First 100,000 |\n48: | [Speed Insights Events](/docs/speed-insights/limits-and-pricing) | 10,000 events over the last 30 days, shared across the team |\n49: | [Web Analytics Events](/docs/analytics/limits-and-pricing#what-is-an-event-in-vercel-web-analytics) | 50,000 events / month included |\n50: | [Workflow Events](/docs/workflows/pricing) | 50,000 events / month included |\n51: | [Workflow Data Written](/docs/workflows/pricing) | 1 GB |\n52: | [Connect Token Requests](/docs/connect/pricing#token-requests) | First 500 |\n53: | [Connect Triggers](/docs/connect/pricing#triggers) | First 1,000 |\n54: ## Hobby billing cycle\n55: As the Hobby plan is a free tier there are no billing cycles. In most cases, if you exceed your usage limits on the Hobby plan, you will have to wait until 30 days have passed before you can use the feature again.\n56: Some usage limits have shorter pause periods:\n57: - [Web Analytics](/docs/analytics/limits-and-pricing#hobby): collection pauses\n58: after the grace period and can resume after 7 days\n59: When your personal account gets converted to a Hobby team, your usage and activity log will be reset. To learn more about this change, read the [changelog](/changelog/2024-01-account-changes).\n60: ## Comparing Hobby and Pro plans\n61: The Pro plan offers more resources and advanced features compared to the Hobby plan. The following table provides a side-by-side comparison of the two plans:\n62: | Feature | Hobby | Pro |\n63: | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n64: | Projects | 200 | Unlimited |\n65: | Vercel Function maximum duration | 300s (5 minutes) | 300s (default) - [configurable up to 800s](/docs/functions/configuring-functions/duration); [extended max duration up to 1800s](/docs/functions/configuring-functions/duration#extended-max-duration-beta) (30 minutes, beta) |\n66: | Build vCPUs | 2 | 4, up to [30](/docs/builds/managing-builds#build-machine-types) |\n67: | Build memory (GB) | 8 | 8GB, up to [60GB](/docs/builds/managing-builds#build-machine-types) |\n68: | Build disk size | 64 GB | 64 GB ([all build machine types](/docs/builds/managing-builds#build-machine-types)) |\n69: | Team collaboration features | - | Yes |\n70: | Domains per project | 50 | Unlimited |\n71: | Deployments per day | 100 | 6,000 |\n72: | Analytics | 50,000 included Events <br />1 month of data | On-demand events <br />Web Analytics Plus add-on |\n73: | Email support | - | Yes |\n74: | [RBAC](/docs/rbac/access-roles) available | N/A | [Owner](/docs/rbac/access-roles#owner-role), [Member](/docs/rbac/access-roles#member-role), [Billing](/docs/rbac/access-roles#billing-role), [Viewer Pro](/docs/rbac/access-roles#pro-viewer-role) |\n75: | [Comments](/docs/comments) | Available | Available for team collaboration |\n76: | [Drains](/docs/drains) | - | [Configurable](/docs/drains/using-drains) (not on a trial) |\n77: | Spend Management | N/A | [Configurable](/docs/spend-management) |\n78: | [Vercel Toolbar](/docs/vercel-toolbar) | Available for certain features | Available |\n79: | [Storage](/docs/storage) | Blob | Blob |\n80: | [Activity Logs](/docs/activity-log) | Available | Available |\n81: | [Runtime Logs](/docs/logs/runtime) | 1 hour of logs | 1 day of logs |\n82: | [DDoS Mitigation](/docs/vercel-firewall/ddos-mitigation) | On by default. Optional [Attack Mode](/docs/vercel-firewall/attack-mode). | On by default. Optional [Attack Mode](/docs/vercel-firewall/attack-mode). |\n83: | [Vercel WAF IP Blocking](/docs/vercel-firewall/vercel-waf/ip-blocking) | Up to 10 | Up to 40 |\n84: | [Vercel WAF Custom Rules](/docs/vercel-firewall/vercel-waf/custom-rules) | Up to 3 | Up to 40 |\n85: | [Deployment Protection](/docs/deployment-protection/usage-and-pricing) | [Vercel Authentication](/docs/deployment-protection/methods-to-protect-deployments/vercel-authentication) for preview and production deployments, [Deployment Protection Exceptions](/docs/deployment-protection/methods-to-bypass-deployment-protection/deployment-protection-exceptions), and [Shareable Links](/docs/deployment-protection/methods-to-bypass-deployment-protection/sharable-links) | The Hobby features, plus [Password Protection](/docs/deployment-protection/methods-to-protect-deployments/password-protection) for $20 per month per protected project |\n86: | [Connect Token Requests](/docs/connect/pricing#token-requests) | 500 included | Unlimited (on-demand) |\n87: | [Connect Triggers](/docs/connect/pricing#triggers) | 1,000 included | Unlimited (on-demand) |\n88: ## Upgrading to Pro\n89: You can take advantage of Vercel's Pro trial to explore [Pro features](/docs/plans/pro-plan) for free during the trial period, with some [limitations](/docs/plans/pro-plan/trials#trial-limitations).\n90: The [free first-year domain offer](/docs/plans/pro-plan#free-first-year-domain-with-pro) is not available during the Pro trial. It applies to paid Pro teams: a team becomes eligible once it is on a paid Pro plan.\n91: To upgrade from a Hobby plan:\n92: 1. Go to your [dashboard](/dashboard). If you're upgrading a team, make sure to select the team you want to upgrade\n93: 2. Open **Settings** in the sidebar and select [**Billing**](https://vercel.com/d?to=%2F%5Bteam%5D%2F%7E%2Fsettings%2Fbilling\\&title=Go+to+Billing)\n94: 3. Under **Plan**, if your team is eligible for an upgrade, you can click the **Upgrade** button. Or, you may need to create or select a team to upgrade. In that case, you can click **Create a Team** or **Upgrade a Team**\n95: 4. Optionally, add team members. Developer seats cost **$20 per user / month**, while Viewer seats are free\n96: 5. Enter your card details\n97: 6. Click **Confirm and Upgrade**\n98: If you would like to end your paid plan, you can [downgrade to Hobby](/docs/plans/pro-plan#downgrading-to-hobby).\n99: ## Search the docs from your terminal\n100: Search the Vercel docs and read pages as Markdown with the Vercel CLI. No login required.\n101: ```bash\n102: # Find docs pages by keyword\n103: npx vercel@latest docs search \"environment variables\"\n104: npx vercel@latest docs search \"function timeout\"\n105: # Print a docs page as Markdown, by path or URL\n106: npx vercel@latest docs inspect <page>\n107: ```\n108: ---\n109: [View full sitemap](/docs/sitemap)\n110: If you encounter incorrect information, can’t find what you need, need a capability Vercel doesn’t currently offer, or have any other feedback to report, please do it by following the instructions at https://vercel.com/feedback.md."
