try a Pages deployment\n7119: POST/accounts/{account_id}/pages/projects/{project_name}/deployments/{deployment_id}/retry\n7120: Roll back a Pages deployment\n7121: POST/accounts/{account_id}/pages/projects/{project_name}/deployments/{deployment_id}/rollback\n7122: PagesProjectsDeploymentsHistory\n7123: PagesProjectsDeploymentsHistoryLogs\n7124: Get Pages deployment logs\n7125: GET/accounts/{account_id}/pages/projects/{project_name}/deployments/{deployment_id}/history/logs\n7126: PagesProjectsDeploymentsTails\n7127: Create deployment tail\n7128: POST/accounts/{account_id}/pages/projects/{project_name}/deployments/{deployment_id}/tails\n7129: Delete deployment tail\n7130: DELETE/accounts/{account_id}/pages/projects/{project_name}/deployments/{deployment_id}/tails/{tail_id}\n7131: PagesProjectsDomains\n7132: List Pages custom domains\n7133: GET/accounts/{account_id}/pages/projects/{project_name}/domains\n7134: Get a Pages custom domain\n7135: GET/accounts/{account_id}/pages/projects/{project_name}/domains/{domain_name}\n7136: Add a Pages custom domain\n7137: POST/accounts/{account_id}/pages/projects/{project_name}/domains\n7138: Retry custom domain validation\n7139: PATCH/accounts/{account_id}/pages/projects/{project_name}/domains/{domain_name}\n7140: Delete a Pages custom domain\n7141: DELETE/accounts/{account_id}/pages/projects/{project_name}/domains/{domain_name}\n7142: PagesAssets\n7143: Upsert asset hashes\n7144: POST/pages/assets/upsert-hashes\n7145: Check missing assets\n7146: POST/pages/assets/check-missing\n7147: Upload asset\n7148: POST/pages/assets/upload\n7149: Registrar\n7150: Registrar API for searching, checking, registering, and managing domains through Cloudflare Registrar.\n7151: Prerequisites\n7152: Before using this API, ensure:\n7153: Cloudflare account — the caller must have a valid Cloudflare account.\n7154: Billing profile — the account must have a billing profile with a valid,\n7155: current default payment method (credit card or other accepted method).\n7156: This cannot be set up via API — the account owner must configure billing\n7157: at https://dash.cloudflare.com/{account_id}/billing/payment-info before\n7158: calling POST /registrations.\n7159: API authentication — use an API token or API key with the appropriate\n7160: Registrar permissions for the operations you are calling.\n7161: Terminology: domain extension\n7162: Throughout this API, “extension” refers to the domain extension part of a fully\n7163: qualified domain name — the portion after the registrable label. For example,\n7164: in example.co.uk, the extension is co.uk (not just uk). This covers both\n7165: top-level domains like com and multi-level extensions like co.uk. This is\n7166: distinct from other uses of the word “extension” (e.g., EPP extensions).\n7167: Supported extensions\n7168: This API supports programmatic registration for all extensions supported by\n7169: the dashboard experience, with the following exceptions:\n7170: giving, mom, inc, lol, sh, link, cc, new\n7171: Cloudflare Registrar supports 400+ extensions in the dashboard. Extensions\n7172: listed above can be registered at https://dash.cloudflare.com/{account_id}/domains/registrations.\n7173: Typical workflow\n7174: Search — call GET /domain-search?q={keyword} to discover available domains.\n7175: Check — call POST /domain-check with candidate domains to verify real-time\n7176: availability and pricing.\n7177: Review the response — if registrable: false, inspect reason to\n7178: understand whether the domain is unavailable, the extension is not supported\n7179: by this API, the extension is not supported by Cloudflare Registrar at all,\n7180: or the extension’s registry has frozen new registrations.\n7181: Handle premium domains — if tier: premium, premium registration is\n7182: not currently supported by this API. Surface the premium pricing to the user,\n7183: but do not proceed to POST /registrations for that domain.\n7184: Observe the registration schema — call GET /extensions/:extension_name\n7185: to discover the required values for registering this extension.\n7186: Register — call POST /registrations with the chosen domain name for\n7187: supported non-premium registrations.\n7188: Confirm completion — if the response is 201 Created, registration\n7189: completed within the default timeout and no polling is needed.\n7190: Poll when needed — if the response is 202 Accepted, poll\n7191: links.self from the workflow response.\n7192: Stop for user action — if state: action_required, stop polling and\n7193: surface context.action to the user.\n7194: The workflow will not resolve on its own.\n7195: Continue when blocked — if state: blocked, continue polling and\n7196: inform the user that a third party, such as the extension registry or losing\n7197: registrar, is delaying progress.\n7198: Review failures before retrying — if state: failed, review\n7199: error.code and error.message, then decide whether user action or a new\n7200: Check call is needed.\n7201: All successful domain registrations are non-refundable. Once the registration\n7202: workflow completes with state: succeeded, the charge cannot be reversed.\n7203: Confirm pricing and domain choice with the user before calling POST /registrations.\n7204: Default behavior for mutating operations\n7205: By default, mutating operations such as create and update hold the connection\n7206: for a bounded, server-defined amount of time while the operation completes.\n7207: In most cases, the response contains a completed workflow status and no\n7208: polling is required.\n7209: Completed within the synchronous wait window: Returns 201 (create)\n7210: or 200 (update) with a workflow_status where state: succeeded and\n7211: completed: true.\n7212: Still processing after the synchronous wait window: Returns\n7213: 202 Accepted with a workflow_status where completed: false. Use\n7214: the links.self URL to poll for completion.\n7215: Non-blocking mode\n7216: To receive an immediate 202 Accepted response without waiting, send the\n7217: Prefer: respond-async request header (RFC 7240). The server will acknowledge\n7218: it with a Preference-Applied: respond-async response header.\n7219: Polling\n7220: When the response is 202, poll the workflow status endpoint indicated by\n7221: links.self in the response body until the workflow reaches a terminal\n7222: state or requires user action.\n7223: Search for available domains\n7224: GET/accounts/{account_id}/registrar/domain-search\n7225: Check domain availability\n7226: POST/accounts/{account_id}/registrar/domain-check\n7227: Check domain transfer eligibility\n7228: POST/accounts/{account_id}/registrar/domain-transfer-check\n7229: RegistrarRegistrations\n7230: Create Registration\n7231: POST/accounts/{account_id}/registrar/registrations\n7232: List Registrations\n7233: GET/accounts/{account_id}/registrar/registrations\n7234: Get Registration\n7235: GET/accounts/{account_id}/registrar/registrations/{domain_name}\n7236: Update Registration\n7237: PATCH/accounts/{account_id}/registrar/registrations/{domain_name}\n7238: RegistrarRegistration Status\n7239: Get Registration Status\n7240: GET/accounts/{account_id}/registrar/registrations/{domain_name}/registration-status\n7241: RegistrarUpdate Status\n7242: Get Update Status\n7243: GET/accounts/{account_id}/registrar/registrations/{domain_name}/update-status\n7244: RegistrarExtensions\n7245: List extensions\n7246: GET/accounts/{account_id}/registrar/extensions\n7247: Get extension\n7248: GET/accounts/{account_id}/registrar/extensions/{extension}\n7249: RegistrarTransfer In\n7250: Initiate Transfer\n7251: POST/accounts/{account_id}/registrar/registrations/{domain_name}/transfer-in\n7252: RegistrarTransfer In Status\n7253: Get Transfer Status\n7254: GET/accounts/{account_id}/registrar/registrations/{domain_name}/transfer-in-status\n7255: Registrar Sandbox\n7256: Use the Registrar Sandbox API to test domain search, availability checks,\n7257: registration, and domain management flows without buying real domains.\n7258: This API is a test environment for the production Registrar API.\n7259: Prerequisites\n7260: Before using this API, make sure you have:\n7261: Cloudflare account — the caller must have a valid Cloudflare account.\n7262: API authentication — create an API token with Registrar Sandbox permissions.\n7263: How the Sandbox API differs from the production Registrar API\n7264: Because the Sandbox API is intended for testing, it behaves differently from\n7265: the production Registrar API in a few important ways:\n7266: No billing — you will not be charged real money for purchasing a domain.\n7267: No real domains — purchased domains are test records and will not be\n7268: reachable on the Internet.\n7269: No DNS zones — purchasing a domain does not create a zone resource.\n7270: No Registration Express Mode — you must provide full contact data.\n7271: Sandbox purchases are still persisted. If you purchase a domain in the sandbox,\n7272: that domain will not be available for others to purchase in the sandbox.\n7273: Terminology: domain extension\n7274: Throughout this API, “extension” refers to the domain extension part of a fully\n7275: qualified domain name — the portion after the registrable label. For example,\n7276: in example.co.uk, the extension is co.uk (not just uk). This covers both\n7277: top-level domains like com and multi-level extensions like co.uk. This is\n7278: distinct from other uses of the word “extension” (e.g., EPP extensions).\n7279: Supported extensions\n7280: The Sandbox API currently supports programmatic registration for these\n7281: extensions:\n7282: com, net\n7283: The production Registrar API supports 40+ extensions.\n7284: Cloudflare Registrar supports 400+ extensions in the dashboard. Extensions\n7285: not listed above can be registered at https://dash.cloudflare.com/{account_id}/domains/registrations.\n7286: Typical workflow\n7287: Search — call GET /domain-search?q={keyword} to discover available domains.\n7288: Check — call POST /domain-check with candidate domains to verify real-time\n7289: availability and pricing.\n7290: Review the response — if registrable: false, inspect reason to\n7291: understand whether the domain is unavailable, the extension is not supported\n7292: by this API, the extension is not supported by Cloudflare Registrar at all,\n7293: or the extension’s registry has frozen new registrations.\n7294: Handle premium domains — if tier: premium, premium registration is\n7295: not currently supported by this API. The Sandbox API currently supports\n7296: only com and net, which do not have premium registrations, but clients\n7297: should still handle this response for consistency with the production\n7298: Registrar API. Surface the premium pricing to the user, but do not proceed\n7299: to POST /registrations for that domain.\n7300: Observe the registration schema — call GET /extensions/:extension_name\n7301: to discover the required values for registering this extension.\n7302: Register — call POST /registrations with the chosen domain name for\n7303: supported non-premium registrations.\n7304: Confirm completion — if the response is 201 Created, registration\n7305: completed within the default timeout and no polling is needed.\n7306: Poll when needed — if the response is 202 Accepted, poll\n7307: links.self from the workflow response.\n7308: Stop for user action — if state: action_required, stop polling and\n7309: surface context.action to the user.\n7310: The workflow will not resolve on its own.\n7311: Continue when blocked — if state: blocked, continue polling and\n7312: inform the user that a third party, such as the extension registry or losing\n7313: registrar, is delaying progress.\n7314: Review failures before retrying — if state: failed, review\n7315: error.code and error.message, then decide whether user action or a new\n7316: Check call is needed.\n7317: Default behavior for mutating operations\n7318: By default, mutating operations such as create and update hold the connection\n7319: for a bounded, server-defined amount of time while the operation completes.\n7320: In most cases, the response contains a completed workflow status and no\n7321: polling is required.\n7322: Completed within the synchronous wait window: Returns 201 (create)\n7323: or 200 (update) with a workflow_status where state: succeeded and\n7324: completed: true.\n7325: Still processing after the synchronous wait window: Returns\n7326: 202 Accepted with a workflow_status where completed: false. Use\n7327: the links.self URL to poll for completion.\n7328: Non-blocking mode\n7329: To receive an immediate 202 Accepted response without waiting, send the\n7330: Prefer: respond-async request header (RFC 7240). The server will acknowledge\n7331: it with a Preference-Applied: respond-async response header.\n7332: Polling\n7333: When the response is 202, poll the workflow status endpoint indicated by\n7334: links.self in the response body until the workflow reaches a terminal\n7335: state or requires user action.\n7336: Search for available domains\n7337: GET/accounts/{account_id}/registrar-sandbox/domain-search\n7338: Check domain availability\n7339: POST/accounts/{account_id}/registrar-sandbox/domain-check\n7340: Registrar SandboxRegistrations\n7341: Create Registration\n7342: POST/accounts/{account_id}/registrar-sandbox/registrations\n7343: List Registrations\n7344: GET/accounts/{account_id}/registrar-sandbox/registrations\n7345: Get Registration\n7346: GET/accounts/{account_id}/registrar-sandbox/registrations/{domain_name}\n7347: Update Registration\n7348: PATCH/accounts/{account_id}/registrar-sandbox/registrations/{domain_name}\n7349: Registrar SandboxRegistration Status\n7350: Get Registration Status\n7351: GET/accounts/{account_id}/registrar-sandbox/registrations/{domain_name}/registration-status\n7352: Registrar SandboxUpdate Status\n7353: Get Update Status\n7354: GET/accounts/{account_id}/registr