      "numbered_text": "1: Data REST API | Supabase Docs\n2: Skip to content\n3: DOCS\n4: Start\n5: Products\n6: Build\n7: Manage\n8: Reference\n9: Resources\n10: DOCS\n11: Search\n12: CtrlK Ask AI Main menu\n13: Open menu\n14: Main menu\n15: StartProductsBuildManageReferenceResources\n16: Products\n17: Features\n18: DatabaseAuthStorageEdge FunctionsRealtime\n19: Modules\n20: Data API (REST)AI & VectorsCronQueuesGraphQL API\n21: Data REST API\n22: Overview\n23: Quickstart\n24: Client Libraries\n25: SecuritySecurity\n26: Securing your API\n27: Custom Claims & RBAC\n28: ToolsTools\n29: Auto-generated Docs\n30: SQL to REST API Translator\n31: GuidesGuides\n32: Creating API routes\n33: Generating TypeScript Types\n34: Generating Python Types\n35: Error Codes\n36: Using the Data APIsUsing the Data APIs\n37: Managing tables and data\n38: Views\n39: Querying joins and nested tables\n40: JSON and unstructured data\n41: Managing database functions\n42: Using full-text search\n43: Query plans with explain()\n44: Using custom schemas\n45: Converting from SQL to JavaScript API\n46: DebuggingDebugging\n47: Handling Errors in supabase-js\n48: DOCS\n49: Start\n50: Products\n51: Build\n52: Manage\n53: Reference\n54: Resources\n55: DOCS\n56: Search\n57: CtrlK Ask AI Main menu\n58: Open menu\n59: Updated Nov 18, 2026\n60: Data REST API\n61: Supabase auto-generates an API directly from your database schema allowing you to connect to your database through a restful interface, directly from the browser.\n62: The API is auto-generated from your database and is designed to get you building as fast as possible, without writing a single line of code.\n63: You can use them directly from the browser (two-tier architecture), or as a complement to your own API server (three-tier architecture).\n64: Looking for your Data API URL and Keys?\n65: You can find the API URL in the Integrations > Data API section of the Dashboard.\n66: You can find the API Keys in the Settings > API Keys section of the Dashboard.\n67: Features\n68: Supabase provides a RESTful API using PostgREST, a thin API layer on top of Postgres.\n69: It exposes everything you need from a CRUD API at the URL https://<project_ref>.supabase.co/rest/v1/.\n70: The REST interface is automatically reflected from your database's schema and is:\n71: Instant and auto-generated: As you update your database the changes are immediately accessible through your API.\n72: Self documenting: Supabase generates documentation in the Dashboard which updates as you make database changes.\n73: Secure: The API is configured to work with Postgres's Row Level Security, provisioned behind an API gateway with key-auth enabled.\n74: Fast: Our benchmarks for basic reads are more than 300% faster than Firebase. The API is a very thin layer on top of Postgres, which does most of the heavy lifting.\n75: Scalable: The API can serve thousands of simultaneous requests, and works well for Serverless workloads.\n76: The reflected API is designed to retain as much of Postgres' capability as possible including:\n77: Basic CRUD operations (Create/Read/Update/Delete)\n78: Arbitrarily deep relationships among tables/views, functions that return table types can also nest related tables/views.\n79: Works with Postgres Views, Materialized Views and Foreign Tables\n80: Works with Postgres Functions\n81: User defined computed columns and computed relationships\n82: The Postgres security model - including Row Level Security, Roles, and Grants.\n83: The REST API resolves all requests to a single SQL statement leading to fast response times and high throughput.\n84: Edit this page\n85: Is this helpful?\n86: No Yes\n87: AI tools\n88: Connect your AI agentAsk ChatGPTAsk ClaudeCopy as MarkdownPrefer on Google\n89: Need some help?\n90: Contact support\n91: Latest product updates?\n92: See Changelog\n93: Something's not right?\n94: Check system status\n95: © Supabase Inc—Do Not Sell or Share My Personal InformationContributingAuthor StyleguideOpen SourceSupaSquad\n96: Twitter\n97: GitHub\n98: Discord\n99: Youtube\n100: Data REST API\n101: Overview"
