      "numbered_text": "1: Authorize requests - Query API\n2: Docs\n3: Docs\n4: Neo4j DBMS\n5: Getting Started\n6: Operations\n7: Migration and Upgrade\n8: Status Codes\n9: Java Reference\n10: Kerberos Add-on\n11: Neo4j Aura\n12: Neo4j Tools\n13: Neo4j Bloom\n14: Neo4j Browser\n15: Neo4j Data Importer\n16: Neo4j Desktop\n17: Neo4j Enterprise Studio\n18: Neo4j Ops Manager\n19: Neodash commercial\n20: Neo4j Graph Data Science\n21: Neo4j Graph Data Science Library\n22: Neo4j Graph Data Science Client\n23: Neo4j Graph Analytics for Snowflake\n24: Cypher Query Language\n25: Cypher\n26: Cypher Cheat Sheet\n27: APOC Library\n28: Generative AI\n29: Neo4j GraphRAG for Python\n30: Embeddings and vector indexes tutorial\n31: GenAI plugin\n32: Vector search indexes\n33: Vector search functions\n34: GraphQL vector index search documentation\n35: Create applications\n36: Python Driver\n37: Go Driver\n38: Java Driver\n39: JDBC Driver\n40: JavaScript Driver\n41: .Net Driver\n42: Neo4j GraphQL Library\n43: Neo4j Visualization Library\n44: OGM Library\n45: Spring Data Neo4j\n46: HTTP API\n47: Neo4j Query API\n48: Bolt\n49: Connect data sources\n50: Neo4j Connector for Apache Spark\n51: Neo4j Connector for Apache Kafka\n52: Change Data Capture (CDC)\n53: BigQuery to Neo4j\n54: Google Cloud to Neo4j\n55: Labs\n56: GenAI Ecosystem\n57: LLM Knowledge Graph Builder\n58: Vector Index & Search\n59: LangChain\n60: LangChain.js\n61: LlamaIndex\n62: Haystack\n63: DSPy\n64: Developer Tools\n65: APOC Extended\n66: Aura CLI\n67: arrows.app\n68: Cypher Workbench\n69: ETL Tool\n70: NeoDash\n71: Frameworks & Integrations\n72: Needle Starter Kit\n73: Neo4j Plugin for Liquibase\n74: Neo4j Migrations\n75: neomodel\n76: RDF & Linked Data\n77: Neosemantics (Java)\n78: RDFLib-Neo4j (Python)\n79: Get Help\n80: Community Forum\n81: Discord Chat\n82: Product Support\n83: Neo4j Developer Blog\n84: Neo4j Videos\n85: GraphAcademy\n86: Beginners Courses\n87: Neo4j Fundamentals\n88: Cypher Fundamentals\n89: Importing Data Fundamentals\n90: Importing CSV Data\n91: Graph Data Modeling\n92: Data Scientist Courses\n93: Get started with Graph Data Science\n94: Path Finding\n95: Generative AI Courses\n96: Neo4j & Generative AI Fundamentals\n97: Vector Indexes & Unstructured Data\n98: Constructing Knowledge Graphs\n99: Building Agents in Neo4j Aura\n100: Neo4j Certification\n101: Neo4j Certified Professional\n102: Neo4j Graph Data Science Certification\n103: Get Started Free\n104: Theme\n105: Light\n106: Dark\n107: Search\n108: Skip to content\n109: Query API\n110: Introduction\n111: Authorize requests\n112: Query the database\n113: Run transactions\n114: Route queries to read cluster members\n115: Retrieve query counters\n116: Profile queries\n117: Coordinate transactions and enforce causal consistency\n118: Run queries as a different user\n119: Stream results\n120: Reference\n121: Endpoints\n122: Headers\n123: Result formats & Data types\n124: Plain JSON\n125: Typed JSON\n126: Changelog\n127: Is this page helpful?\n128: Query API\n129: Authorize requests\n130: Raise an issue\n131: Authorize requests\n132: Unless authentication is disabled on the server, all requests must be authorized using the login credentials of a valid user.\n133: Request are authorized through an Authorization header.\n134: Both basic and bearer authentication are supported.\n135: If authentication is disabled on the server, requests can be sent without an Authorization header.\n136: Basic authentication\n137: The header format for basic authentication follows the standard format (RFC 7617), with UTF-8 encoding:\n138: Authorization: Basic <base64(<username>:<password>)>\n139: Example 1. Basic authentication\n140: To authenticate as user neo4j with password verysecret, first join them with a colon:\n141: neo4j:verysecret\n142: and then base64-encode that value:\n143: bmVvNGo6dmVyeXNlY3JldA==\n144: How to base64-encode a string\n145: To base64-encode a string on a Linux or Mac machine, use the built-in base64 command:\n146: echo -n \"neo4j:verysecret\" | base64\n147: To obtain the final header, prepend Basic to the base64-encoding of the credentials:\n148: Authorization: Basic bmVvNGo6dmVyeXNlY3JldA==\n149: Bearer authentication\n150: The header format to authenticate with a bearer token is:\n151: Authorization: Bearer <token>\n152: where <token> is base64-encoded. Most services provide tokens already base64-decoded, so ensure you don’t base64-encode them again.\n153: Bearer authentication with token eGJoa2pubHZpYW56dGdocXdhd3hxZmUK\n154: Authorization: Bearer eGJoa2pubHZpYW56dGdocXdhd3hxZmUK\n155: It is up to your application to generate bearer tokens via your SSO provider.\n156: The Neo4j server should also be set up to work with SSO.\n157: For more information, see Configuring Neo4j Single Sign-On (SSO).\n158: Authentication realm\n159: Introduced in 2026.10\n160: You can define an authentication context for both Basic and Bearer authentication. Specify the realm with the header Neo4j-Realm:\n161: Neo4j-Realm: <realm>\n162: To authenticate against a specific realm (for example an LDAP realm named ldap-users), include the realm alongside your authorization credentials:\n163: Using authentication realm\n164: Authorization: Basic bmVvNGo6dmVyeXNlY3JldA==\n165: Neo4j-Realm: ldap-users\n166: Errors\n167: Missing authorization\n168: If an Authorization header is not supplied (and authentication is not disabled), the server replies with status 401 Forbidden and an error.\n169: Example request\n170: POST http://localhost:7474/db/neo4j/query/v2\n171: Example response\n172: 401: Unauthorized\n173: Content-Type: application/json\n174: {\n175: \"errors\" : [ {\n176: \"code\" : \"Neo.ClientError.Security.Unauthorized\",\n177: \"message\" : \"No authentication header supplied.\"\n178: } ]\n179: }\n180: Incorrect authentication\n181: If an incorrect username or password is provided, the server replies with status 401 Forbidden and an error.\n182: Example request\n183: POST http://localhost:7474/db/neo4j/query/v2\n184: Authorization: Basic bmVvNGo6aW5jb3JyZWN0\n185: Example response\n186: 401: Unauthorized\n187: Content-Type: application/json\n188: {\n189: \"errors\" : [ {\n190: \"code\" : \"Neo.ClientError.Security.Unauthorized\",\n191: \"message\" : \"Invalid username or password.\"\n192: } ]\n193: }\n194: Invalid authentication\n195: If the content of the Authorization header is not properly base64-encoded, the server replies with status 401 Forbidden and an error.\n196: Example request\n197: POST http://localhost:7474/db/neo4j/query/v2\n198: Authorization: Basic not-proper-base64\n199: Example response\n200: 401: Unauthorized\n201: Content-Type: application/json\n202: {\n203: \"errors\" : [ {\n204: \"code\": \"Neo.ClientError.Request.InvalidFormat\",\n205: \"message\": \"Invalid authentication header.\"\n206: } ]\n207: }\n208: Introduction\n209: Query the database\n210: Products\n211: Neo4j Graph Database\n212: Neo4j AuraDB\n213: Neo4j Graph Data Science\n214: Deployment Center\n215: Professional Services\n216: Pricing\n217: Developers\n218: Developer Home\n219: Documentation\n220: Deployment Center\n221: Developer Blog\n222: Community\n223: Virtual Events\n224: GraphAcademy\n225: Learn\n226: Resource Library\n227: Neo4j Blog\n228: GraphAcademy\n229: Research Center\n230: Case Studies\n231: Events Calendar\n232: NODES 2026\n233: Webinars\n234: Company\n235: About Us\n236: Newsroom\n237: Awards and Honors\n238: Careers\n239: Culture\n240: Leadership\n241: Support\n242: Social Networks\n243: © 2026 Neo4j, Inc.\n244: Terms | Privacy Policy | Sitemap\n245: Neo4j®, Neo Technology®, Cypher®, Neo4j® Bloom™, Neo4j® AuraDB℠ and\n246: Neo4j® AuraDS℠ are registered trademarks\n247: of Neo4j, Inc. All other marks are owned by their respective companies."
