      "numbered_text": "1: Introduction - Neo4j MCP\n2: Docs\n3: Docs\n4: Neo4j DBMS\n5: Getting Started\n6: Operations\n7: Migration and Upgrade\n8: Data Ingestion Guide\n9: Status Codes\n10: Java Reference\n11: Kerberos Add-on\n12: Neo4j Aura\n13: Neo4j Tools\n14: Neo4j Bloom\n15: Neo4j Browser\n16: Neo4j Data Importer\n17: Neo4j Desktop\n18: Neo4j Enterprise Studio\n19: Neo4j Ops Manager\n20: Neodash commercial\n21: Neo4j Graph Data Science\n22: Neo4j Graph Data Science Library\n23: Neo4j Graph Data Science Client\n24: Neo4j Graph Analytics for Snowflake\n25: Cypher Query Language\n26: Cypher\n27: Cypher Cheat Sheet\n28: APOC Library\n29: Generative AI\n30: Neo4j GraphRAG for Python\n31: Embeddings and vector indexes tutorial\n32: GenAI plugin\n33: Vector search indexes\n34: Vector search functions\n35: GraphQL vector index search documentation\n36: Create applications\n37: Python Driver\n38: Go Driver\n39: Java Driver\n40: JDBC Driver\n41: JavaScript Driver\n42: .Net Driver\n43: MCP\n44: Neo4j GraphQL Library\n45: Neo4j Visualization Library\n46: OGM Library\n47: Spring Data Neo4j\n48: HTTP API\n49: Neo4j Query API\n50: Bolt\n51: Connect data sources\n52: Neo4j Connector for Apache Spark\n53: Neo4j Connector for Apache Kafka\n54: Change Data Capture (CDC)\n55: BigQuery to Neo4j\n56: Google Cloud to Neo4j\n57: Labs\n58: GenAI Ecosystem\n59: LLM Knowledge Graph Builder\n60: Vector Index & Search\n61: LangChain\n62: LangChain.js\n63: LlamaIndex\n64: Haystack\n65: DSPy\n66: Agent Memory\n67: Getting Started\n68: Tutorials\n69: Framework Integrations\n70: MCP Server\n71: Developer Tools\n72: APOC Extended\n73: Aura CLI\n74: arrows.app\n75: Cypher Workbench\n76: ETL Tool\n77: NeoDash\n78: Frameworks & Integrations\n79: Needle Starter Kit\n80: Neo4j Plugin for Liquibase\n81: Neo4j Migrations\n82: neomodel\n83: RDF & Linked Data\n84: Neosemantics (Java)\n85: RDFLib-Neo4j (Python)\n86: Get Help\n87: Community Forum\n88: Discord Chat\n89: Product Support\n90: Neo4j Developer Blog\n91: Neo4j Videos\n92: GraphAcademy\n93: Beginners Courses\n94: Neo4j Fundamentals\n95: Cypher Fundamentals\n96: Importing Data Fundamentals\n97: Importing CSV Data\n98: Graph Data Modeling\n99: Data Scientist Courses\n100: Get started with Graph Data Science\n101: Path Finding\n102: Generative AI Courses\n103: Neo4j & Generative AI Fundamentals\n104: Vector Indexes & Unstructured Data\n105: Constructing Knowledge Graphs\n106: Building Agents in Neo4j Aura\n107: Neo4j Certification\n108: Neo4j Certified Professional\n109: Neo4j Graph Data Science Certification\n110: Get Started Free\n111: Theme\n112: Light\n113: Dark\n114: Search\n115: Skip to content\n116: Neo4j MCP\n117: Product Version\n118: Version 2 (Current)\n119: Version 1\n120: Neo4j MCP\n121: Introduction\n122: Quickstart\n123: Tools\n124: Security\n125: Setup\n126: MCP for Aura\n127: Installation\n128: Client configuration\n129: HTTP Authentication\n130: HTTP mode\n131: Configuration reference\n132: STDIO configuration\n133: HTTP configuration\n134: Requirement checks\n135: Monitoring\n136: Logging\n137: Telemetry\n138: Versions and support\n139: Migrate from v1 to v2\n140: Known issues\n141: Is this page helpful?\n142: Neo4j MCP\n143: Introduction\n144: Raise an issue\n145: Introduction\n146: Neo4j MCP implements the Model Context Protocol (MCP), an open standard that lets applications connect to external data sources and tools.\n147: It bridges any MCP-compatible client and your Neo4j instance, giving that client direct, structured access to your graph database.\n148: AI assistants and agents are the most common MCP clients today, tools like Claude, Cursor, or VS Code with MCP support.\n149: But MCP itself doesn’t require AI.\n150: Any application that implements the MCP client specification can connect to Neo4j through it, whether or not a model is involved.\n151: Neo4j MCP is built for:\n152: Developers who want to query Neo4j conversationally while prototyping.\n153: Data scientists and analysts exploring graph data without deep Cypher® expertise.\n154: Platform teams deploying shared tooling that needs structured, auditable access to Neo4j.\n155: Application builders using Neo4j as a knowledge source or reasoning backend, including in multi-agent systems.\n156: A connected client can:\n157: Explore your graph schema - discover node labels, relationship types, and property keys, and reason about your data model without knowing it in advance.\n158: Run Cypher queries - execute reads and writes against your database from natural language prompts or programmatic calls.\n159: Inspect and analyze data - retrieve nodes, relationships, and paths to answer questions, generate summaries, or feed other workflows.\n160: Prerequisites\n161: A running Neo4j database instance. Options include Aura, neo4j-desktop or self-managed.\n162: The APOC plugin installed in the Neo4j instance.\n163: Any MCP-compatible client, e.g. VSCode with MCP support.\n164: Optional requirements\n165: The Graph Data Science (GDS) library is optional.\n166: See GDS requirement for details.\n167: Examples for natural language prompts\n168: Here are some example prompts you can try in Copilot or any other MCP client:\n169: \"What does my Neo4j instance contain? List all node labels, relationship types, and property keys.\"\n170: \"Find all Person nodes and their relationships in my Neo4j instance.\"\n171: \"Create a new User node with a name 'John' in my Neo4j instance.\"\n172: Quickstart\n173: Products\n174: Neo4j Graph Database\n175: Neo4j AuraDB\n176: Neo4j Graph Data Science\n177: Deployment Center\n178: Professional Services\n179: Pricing\n180: Developers\n181: Developer Home\n182: Documentation\n183: Deployment Center\n184: Developer Blog\n185: Community\n186: Virtual Events\n187: GraphAcademy\n188: Learn\n189: Resource Library\n190: Neo4j Blog\n191: GraphAcademy\n192: Research Center\n193: Case Studies\n194: Events Calendar\n195: NODES 2026\n196: Webinars\n197: Company\n198: About Us\n1