      "numbered_text": "1: API Authentication | Sentry Docs\n2: Skip to content\n3: Docs\n4: Get Started\n5: SDKs\n6: Product\n7: AI\n8: Concepts\n9: API\n10: Manage\n11: Ask AI\n12: Go to Sentry\n13: Open Main Menu\n14: API Reference\n15: Authentication\n16: Paginating Results\n17: Permissions & Scopes\n18: Rate Limits\n19: Requests\n20: Crons\n21: Dashboards\n22: Discover & Performance\n23: Environments\n24: Events & Issues\n25: Explore\n26: Flags\n27: Integration Platform\n28: Integrations\n29: Investigations\n30: Mobile Builds\n31: Monitors & Alerts\n32: Notebooks\n33: Organizations\n34: Profiling\n35: Projects\n36: Releases\n37: Replays\n38: SCIM\n39: Seer\n40: Snapshots\n41: Spike Protection Notifications\n42: Teams\n43: Users\n44: Product Changelog\n45: Sandbox\n46: More\n47: Home\n48: API Reference\n49: Authentication\n50: Copy page\n51: API Authentication\n52: Auth Tokens\n53: Authentication tokens are passed using an auth header, and are used to authenticate as a user or organization account with the API. In our documentation, we have several placeholders that appear between curly braces or chevrons, such as {API_KEY} or <auth_token>, which you will need to replace with one of your authentication tokens in order to use the API call effectively.\n54: For the string format of auth tokens, organization tokens, DSNs, and legacy API keys, see Token and Credential Formats.\n55: For example, when the documentation says:\n56: Bash\n57: Copied\n58: curl -H 'Authorization: Bearer {TOKEN}' https://sentry.io/api/0/organizations/{organization_slug}/projects/\n59: curl -H 'Authorization: Bearer {TOKEN}' https://sentry.io/api/0/organizations/{organization_slug}/projects/\n60: If your authentication token is 1a2b3c, and your organization slug is acme then the command should be:\n61: Bash\n62: Copied\n63: curl -H 'Authorization: Bearer 1a2b3c' https://sentry.io/api/0/organizations/acme/projects/\n64: curl -H 'Authorization: Bearer 1a2b3c' https://sentry.io/api/0/organizations/acme/projects/\n65: You can create authentication tokens within Sentry by creating an internal integration. This is also available for self-hosted Sentry.\n66: User authentication tokens\n67: Some API endpoints require an authentication token that's associated with your user account, rather than an authentication token from an internal integration. These auth tokens can be created within Sentry on the \"User settings\" page (User settings > Personal Tokens) and assigned specific scopes.\n68: The endpoints that require a user authentication token are specific to your user, such as Retrieve an Organization.\n69: OAuth2\n70: For third-party applications that need to access Sentry on behalf of users, Sentry supports OAuth2 with the authorization code grant type. This allows users to authorize your application without sharing their credentials.\n71: Authorization Request\n72: Direct users to the authorization endpoint:\n73: Bash\n74: Copied\n75: https://sentry.io/oauth/authorize/?client_id={CLIENT_ID}&response_type=code&scope={SCOPES}\n76: https://sentry.io/oauth/authorize/?client_id={CLIENT_ID}&response_type=code&scope={SCOPES}\n77: Parameters:\n78: ParameterRequiredDescription\n79: client_idYesYour registered client ID\n80: response_typeYesMust be code\n81: scopeYesSpace-separated list of permissions\n82: redirect_uriNoYour callback URI (must match registered URI)\n83: stateNoRandom string to prevent CSRF attacks\n84: code_challengeRecommendedPKCE challenge (see below)\n85: code_challenge_methodRecommendedMust be S256\n86: After the user approves, Sentry redirects to your callback URI with an authorization code:\n87: Bash\n88: Copied\n89: https://your-app.com/callback?code={AUTHORIZATION_CODE}\n90: https://your-app.com/callback?code={AUTHORIZATION_CODE}\n91: Token Exchange\n92: Exchange the authorization code for an access token:\n93: Bash\n94: Copied\n95: curl -X POST https://sentry.io/oauth/token/ \\\n96: -d client_id={CLIENT_ID} \\\n97: -d client_secret={CLIENT_SECRET} \\\n98: -d grant_type=authorization_code \\\n99: -d code={AUTHORIZATION_CODE} \\\n100: -d code_verifier={CODE_VERIFIER}\n101: curl -X POST https://sentry.io/oauth/token/ \\\n102: -d client_id={CLIENT_ID} \\\n103: -d client_secret={CLIENT_SECRET} \\\n104: -d grant_type=authorization_code \\\n105: -d code={AUTHORIZATION_CODE} \\\n106: -d code_verifier={CODE_VERIFIER}\n107: The code_verifier parameter is required if you used PKCE in the authorization request.\n108: Response:\n109: JSON\n110: Copied\n111: {\n112: \"access_token\": \"{ACCESS_TOKEN}\",\n113: \"refresh_token\": \"{REFRESH_TOKEN}\",\n114: \"expires_in\": 2591999,\n115: \"expires_at\": \"2024-11-27T23:20:21.054320Z\",\n116: \"token_type\": \"bearer\",\n117: \"scope\": \"org:read project:read\",\n118: \"user\": {\n119: \"id\": \"123\",\n120: \"name\": \"Jane Doe\",\n121: \"email\": \"jane@example.com\"\n122: }\n123: }\n124: {\n125: \"access_token\": \"{ACCESS_TOKEN}\",\n126: \"refresh_token\": \"{REFRESH_TOKEN}\",\n127: \"expires_in\": 2591999,\n128: \"expires_at\": \"2024-11-27T23:20:21.054320Z\",\n129: \"token_type\": \"bearer\",\n130: \"scope\": \"org:read project:read\",\n131: \"user\": {\n132: \"id\": \"123\",\n133: \"name\": \"Jane Doe\",\n134: \"email\": \"jane@example.com\"\n135: }\n136: }\n137: Refreshing Tokens\n138: Access tokens expire after 30 days. Use the refresh token to obtain new tokens:\n139: Bash\n140: Copied\n141: curl -X POST https://sentry.io/oauth/token/ \\\n142: -d client_id={CLIENT_ID} \\\n143: -d client_secret={CLIENT_SECRET} \\\n144: -d grant_type=refresh_token \\\n145: -d refresh_token={REFRESH_TOKEN}\n146: curl -X POST https://sentry.io/oauth/token/ \\\n147: -d client_id={CLIENT_ID} \\\n148: -d client_secret={CLIENT_SECRET} \\\n149: -d grant_type=refresh_token \\\n150: -d refresh_token={REFRESH_TOKEN}\n151: Using Access Tokens\n152: Include the access token in API requests using the Authorization header:\n153: Bash\n154: Copied\n155: curl -H 'Authorization: Bearer {ACCESS_TOKEN}' \\\n156: https://sentry.io/api/0/organizations/\n157: curl -H 'Authorization: Bearer {ACCESS_TOKEN}' \\\n158: https://sentry.io/api/0/organizations/\n159: Organization Scoping\n160: A Sentry user can belong to multiple organizations. The access token only provides access to the specific organization the user selected during the OAuth flow. The /api/0/organizations/ endpoint will only return the connected organization.\n161: Device Authorization Flow\n162: The device authorization grant (RFC 8628) enables applications on devices without a browser or with limited input capabilities to obtain authorization. This is ideal for CLI tools, CI/CD pipelines, Docker containers, and other headless environments where redirecting to a browser on the same device isn't practical.\n163: How it works: Your application requests a device code, displays a short user code to the user, and polls for authorization. The user visits Sentry in their browser (on any device), enters the code, and approves the request. Once approved, your application receives an access token.\n164: Step 1: Request Device Code\n165: Request a device code from the device authorization endpoint:\n166: Bash\n167: Copied\n168: curl -X POST https://sentry.io/oauth/device/code/ \\\n169: -d client_id={CLIENT_ID} \\\n170: -d scope=org:read%20project:read\n171: curl -X POST https://sentry.io/oauth/device/code/ \\\n172: -d client_id={CLIENT_ID} \\\n173: -d scope=org:read%20project:read\n174: Parameters:\n175: ParameterRequiredDescription\n176: client_idYesYour registered client ID\n177: scopeNoSpace-separated list of permissions\n178: Response:\n179: JSON\n180: Copied\n181: {\n182: \"device_code\": \"a1b2c3d4e5f6...\",\n183: \"user_code\": \"ABCD-EFGH\",\n184: \"verification_uri\": \"https://sentry.io/oauth/device/\",\n185: \"verification_uri_complete\": \"https://sentry.io/oauth/device/?user_code=ABCD-EFGH\",\n186: \"expires_in\": 600,\n187: \"interval\": 5\n188: }\n189: {\n190: \"device_code\": \"a1b2c3d4e5f6...\",\n191: \"user_code\": \"ABCD-EFGH\",\n192: \"verification_uri\": \"https://sentry.io/oauth/device/\",\n193: \"verification_uri_complete\": \"https://sentry.io/oauth/device/?user_code=ABCD-EFGH\",\n194: \"expires_in\": 600,\n195: \"interval\": 5\n196: }\n197: FieldDescription\n198: device_codeSecret code your application uses to poll for the token\n199: user_codeShort code the user enters to authorize (format: XXXX-XXXX)\n200: verification_uriURL where the user should go to enter the code\n201: verification_uri_completeURL with user code pre-filled (useful for QR codes or clickable links)\n202: expires_inSeconds until the codes expire (default: 600 / 10 minutes)\n203: intervalMinimum seconds between polling requests (default: 5)\n204: Step 2: Display Instructions to User\n205: Display the user code and verification URL to your user:\n206: Bash\n207: Copied\n208: To authenticate, visit: https://sentry.io/oauth/device/\n209: Enter code: ABCD-EFGH\n210: To authenticate, visit: https://sentry.io/oauth/device/\n211: Enter code: ABCD-EFGH\n212: The user code uses an unambiguous character set (no 0/O, 1/I/L confusion) for easy entry.\n213: Step 3: Poll for Token\n214: While the user authorizes in their browser, poll the token endpoint:\n215: Bash\n216: Copied\n217: curl -X POST https://sentry.io/oauth/token/ \\\n218: -d client_id={CLIENT_ID} \\\n219: -d device_code={DEVICE_CODE} \\\n220: -d grant_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:device_code\n221: curl -X POST https://sentry.io/oauth/token/ \\\n222: -d client_id={CLIENT_ID} \\\n223: -d device_code={DEVICE_CODE} \\\n224: -d grant_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:device_code\n225: Poll at the interval specified in the device authorization response (default: 5 seconds). While waiting for the user, you'll receive:\n226: JSON\n227: Copied\n228: {\n229: \"error\": \"authorization_pending\",\n230: \"error_description\": \"The authorization request is still pending.\"\n231: }\n232: {\n233: \"error\": \"authorization_pending\",\n234: \"error_description\": \"The authorization request is still pending.\"\n235: }\n236: Continue polling until you receive a token or an error.\n237: Step 4: Receive Access Token\n238: Once the user approves, the token endpoint returns:\n239: JSON\n240: Copied\n241: {\n242: \"access_token\": \"{ACCESS_TOKEN}\",\n243: \"refresh_token\": \"{REFRESH_TOKEN}\",\n244: \"expires_in\": 2591999,\n245: \"expires_at\": \"2024-11-27T23:20:21.054320Z\",\n246: \"token_type\": \"bearer\",\n247: \"scope\": \"org:read project:read\",\n248: \"user\": {\n249: \"id\": \"123\",\n250: \"name\": \"Jane Doe\",\n251: \"email\": \"jane@example.com\"\n252: }\n253: }\n254: {\n255: \"access_token\": \"{ACCESS_TOKEN}\",\n256: \"refresh_token\": \"{REFRESH_TOKEN}\",\n257: \"expires_in\": 2591999,\n258: \"expires_at\": \"2024-11-27T23:20:21.054320Z\",\n259: \"token_type\": \"bearer\",\n260: \"scope\": \"org:read project:read\",\n261: \"user\": {\n262: \"id\": \"123\",\n263: \"name\": \"Jane Doe\",\n264: \"email\": \"jane@example.com\"\n265: }\n266: }\n267: Device Flow Error Responses\n268: ErrorDescriptionAction\n269: authorization_pendingUser hasn't completed authorization yetContinue polling\n270: slow_downPolling too frequentlyIncrease interval by 5 seconds\n271: access_deniedUser denied the authorization requestStop polling, notify user\n272: expired_tokenDevice code has expiredRestart the flow from step 1\n273: Device Flow Example\n274: Python\n275: Copied\n276: import time\n277: import requests\n278: CLIENT_ID = 'your-client-id'\n279: DEVICE_AUTH_URL = 'https://sentry.io/oauth/device/code/'\n280: TOKEN_URL = 'https://sentry.io/oauth/token/'\n281: def authenticate():\n282: # Step 1: Request device code\n283: response = requests.post(DEVICE_AUTH_URL, data={\n284: 'client_id': CLIENT_ID,\n285: 'scope': 'org:read project:read'\n286: })\n287: data = response.json()\n288: device_code = data['device_code']\n289: user_code = data['user_code']\n290: verification_uri = data['verification_uri']\n291: verification_uri_complete = data.get('verification_uri_complete')\n292: interval = data.get('interval', 5)\n293: expires_in = data['expires_in']\n294: # Step 2: Display instructions\n295: print(f\"\\nTo authenticate, visit: {verification_uri}\")\n296: print(f\"Enter code: {user_code}\")\n297: if verification_uri_complete:\n298: print(f\"\\nOr open this link directly: {verification_uri_complete}\")\n299: print()\n300: # Step 3: Poll for token\n301: deadline = time.time() + expires_in\n302: while time.time() < deadline:\n303: time.sleep(interval)\n304: response = requests.post(TOKEN_URL, data={\n305: 'client_id': CLIENT_ID,\n306: 'device_code': device_code,\n307: 'grant_type': 'urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:device_code'\n308: })\n309: result = response.json()\n310: if 'access_token' in result:\n311: # Step 4: Success\n312: print(\"Authentication successful!\")\n313: return result['access_token'], result['refresh_token']\n314: error = result.get('error')\n315: if error == 'authorization_pending':\n316: continue\n317: elif error == 'slow_down':\n318: interval += 5\n319: elif error == 'access_denied':\n320: raise Exception(\"User denied authorization\")\n321: elif error == 'expired_token':\n322: raise Exception(\"Device code expired\")\n323: else:\n324: raise Exception(f\"Unexpected error: {error}\")\n325: raise Exception(\"Authorization timed out\")\n326: if __name__ == '__main__':\n327: access_token, refresh_token = authenticate()\n328: print(f\"Access token: {access_token[:20]}...\")\n329: import time\n330: import requests\n331: CLIENT_ID = 'your-client-id'\n332: DEVICE_AUTH_URL = 'https://sentry.io/oauth/device/code/'\n333: TOKEN_URL = 'https://sentry.io/oauth/token/'\n334: def authenticate():\n335: # Step 1: Request device code\n336: response = requests.post(DEVICE_AUTH_URL, data={\n337: 'client_id': CLIENT_ID,\n338: 'scope': 'org:read project:read'\n339: })\n340: data = response.json()\n341: device_code = data['device_code']\n342: user_code = data['user_code']\n343: verification_uri = data['verification_uri']\n344: verification_uri_complete = data.get('verification_uri_complete')\n345: interval = data.get('interval', 5)\n346: expires_in = data['expires_in']\n347: # Step 2: Display instructions\n348: print(f\"\\nTo authenticate, visit: {verification_uri}\")\n349: print(f\"Enter code: {user_code}\")\n350: if verification_uri_complete:\n351: print(f\"\\nOr open this link directly: {verification_uri_complete}\")\n352: print()\n353: # Step 3: Poll for token\n354: deadline = time.time() + expires_in\n355: while time.time() < deadline:\n356: time.sleep(interval)\n357: response = requests.post(TOKEN_URL, data={\n358: 'client_id': CLIENT_ID,\n359: 'device_code': device_code,\n360: 'grant_type': 'urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:device_code'\n361: })\n362: result = response.json()\n363: if 'access_token' in result:\n364: # Step 4: Success\n365: print(\"Authentication successful!\")\n366: return result['access_token'], result['refresh_token']\n367: error = result.get('error')\n368: if error == 'authorization_pending':\n369: continue\n370: elif error == 'slow_down':\n371: interval += 5\n372: elif error == 'access_denied':\n373: raise Exception(\"User denied authorization\")\n374: elif error == 'expired_token':\n375: raise Exception(\"Device code expired\")\n376: else:\n377: raise Exception(f\"Unexpected error: {error}\")\n378: raise Exception(\"Authorization timed out\")\n379: if __name__ == '__main__':\n380: access_token, refresh_token = authenticate()\n381: print(f\"Access token: {access_token[:20]}...\")\n382: PKCE (Proof Key for Code Exchange)\n383: PKCE protects against authorization code interception attacks and is strongly recommended for all OAuth clients.\n384: How it works: For each authorization request, generate a unique random secret called the code_verifier. Create a code_challenge by hashing this verifier. The challenge is sent with the authorization request, while the original verifier is sent when exchanging the code for a token. Sentry verifies they match, ensuring the same client that started the flow is completing it.\n385: Generating PKCE values (generate fresh for each authorization request):\n386: Python\n387: Copied\n388: import base64\n389: import hashlib\n390: import secrets\n391: # Generate a random code_verifier (43-128 URL-safe characters)\n392: code_verifier = secrets.token_urlsafe(64)\n393: # Create code_challenge by hashing the verifier with SHA256\n394: code_challenge = base64.urlsafe_b64encode(\n395: hashlib.sha256(code_verifier.encode()).digest()\n396: ).rstrip(b'=').decode()\n397: # Store code_verifier securely - you'll need it for the token exchange\n398: import base64\n399: import hashlib\n400: import secrets\n401: # Generate a random code_verifier (43-128 URL-safe characters)\n402: code_verifier = secrets.token_urlsafe(64)\n403: # Create code_challenge by hashing the verifier with SHA256\n404: code_challenge = base64.urlsafe_b64encode(\n405: hashlib.sha256(code_verifier.encode()).digest()\n406: ).rstrip(b'=').decode()\n407: # Store code_verifier securely - you'll need it for the token exchange\n408: Error Handling\n409: Status CodeMeaningAction\n410: 401Token expired or revokedRefresh the token, or prompt user to reconnect\n411: 403Insufficient permissionsRequest additional scopes or handle gracefully\n412: Example Implementation\n413: Python\n414: Copied\n415: import base64\n416: import hashlib\n417: import secrets\n418: import requests\n419: from flask import Flask, redirect, request, session\n420: app = Flask(__name__)\n421: app.secret_key = 'your-secret-key'\n422: CLIENT_ID = 'your-client-id'\n423: CLIENT_SECRET = 'your-client-secret'\n424: REDIRECT_URI = 'https://your-app.com/callback'\n425: TOKEN_URL = 'https://sentry.io/oauth/token/'\n426: def generate_pkce_pair():\n427: \"\"\"Generate a code verifier and challenge for PKCE.\"\"\"\n428: code_verifier = secrets.token_urlsafe(64)\n429: code_challenge = base64.urlsafe_b64encode(\n430: hashlib.sha256(code_verifier.encode()).digest()\n431: ).rstrip(b'=').decode()\n432: return code_verifier, code_challenge\n433: @app.route('/connect')\n434: def connect():\n435: code_verifier, code_challenge = generate_pkce_pair()\n436: session['code_verifier'] = code_verifier\n437: return redirect(\n438: f\"https://sentry.io/oauth/authorize/\"\n439: f\"?client_id={CLIENT_ID}\"\n440: f\"&response_type=code\"\n441: f\"&scope=org:read%20project:read\"\n442: f\"&redirect_uri={REDIRECT_URI}\"\n443: f\"&code_challenge={code_challenge}\"\n444: f\"&code_challenge_method=S256\"\n445: )\n446: @app.route('/callback')\n447: def callback():\n448: code = request.args.get('code')\n449: code_verifier = session.pop('code_verifier', None)\n450: response = requests.post(TOKEN_URL, data={\n451: \"client_id\": CLIENT_ID,\n452: \"client_secret\": CLIENT_SECRET,\n453: \"grant_type\": \"authorization_code\",\n454: \"code\": code,\n455: \"code_verifier\": code_verifier\n456: })\n457: tokens = response.json()\n458: session['access_token'] = tokens['access_token']\n459: session['refresh_token'] = tokens['refresh_token']\n460: return \"Connected!\"\n461: def refresh_token():\n462: response = requests.post(TOKEN_URL, data={\n463: \"client_id\": CLIENT_ID,\n464: \"client_secret\": CLIENT_SECRET,\n465: \"grant_type\": \"refresh_token\",\n466: \"refresh_token\": session['refresh_token']\n467: })\n468: tokens = response.json()\n469: session['access_token'] = tokens['access_token']\n470: session['refresh_token'] = tokens['refresh_token']\n471: import base64\n472: import hashlib\n473: import secrets\n474: import requests\n475: from flask import Flask, redirect, request, session\n476: app = Flask(__name__)\n477: app.secret_key = 'your-secret-key'\n478: CLIENT_ID = 'your-client-id'\n479: CLIENT_SECRET = 'your-client-secret'\n480: REDIRECT_URI = 'https://your-app.com/callback'\n481: TOKEN_URL = 'https://sentry.io/oauth/token/'\n482: def generate_pkce_pair():\n483: \"\"\"Generate a code verifier and challenge for PKCE.\"\"\"\n484: code_verifier = secrets.token_urlsafe(64)\n485: code_challenge = base64.urlsafe_b64encode(\n486: hashlib.sha256(code_verifier.encode()).digest()\n487: ).rstrip(b'=').decode()\n488: return code_verifier, code_challenge\n489: @app.route('/connect')\n490: def connect():\n491: code_verifier, code_challenge = generate_pkce_pair()\n492: session['code_verifier'] = code_verifier\n493: return redirect(\n494: f\"https://sentry.io/oauth/authorize/\"\n495: f\"?client_id={CLIENT_ID}\"\n496: f\"&response_type=code\"\n497: f\"&scope=org:read%20project:read\"\n498: f\"&redirect_uri={REDIRECT_URI}\"\n499: f\"&code_challenge={code_challenge}\"\n500: f\"&code_challenge_method=S256\"\n501: )\n502: @app.route('/callback')\n503: def callback():\n504: code = request.args.get('code')\n505: code_verifier = session.pop('code_verifier', None)\n506: response = requests.post(TOKEN_URL, data={\n507: \"client_id\": CLIENT_ID,\n508: \"client_secret\": CLIENT_SECRET,\n509: \"grant_type\": \"authorization_code\",\n510: \"code\": code,\n511: \"code_verifier\": code_verifier\n512: })\n513: tokens = response.json()\n514: session['access_token'] = tokens['access_token']\n515: session['refresh_token'] = tokens['refresh_token']\n516: return \"Connected!\"\n517: def refresh_token():\n518: response = requests.post(TOKEN_URL, data={\n519: \"client_id\": CLIENT_ID,\n520: \"client_secret\": CLIENT_SECRET,\n521: \"grant_type\": \"refresh_token\",\n522: \"refresh_token\": session['refresh_token']\n523: })\n524: tokens = response.json()\n525: session['access_token'] = tokens['access_token']\n526: session['refresh_token'] = tokens['refresh_token']\n527: DSN Authentication\n528: Some API endpoints may allow DSN-based authentication. This is generally very limited and an endpoint will describe if its supported. This works similar to Bearer token authentication, but uses your DSN (Client Key).\n529: Bash\n530: Copied\n531: curl -H 'Authorization: DSN {DSN}' https://sentry.io/api/0/{organization_slug}/{project_slug}/user-reports/\n532: curl -H 'Authorization: DSN {DSN}' https://sentry.io/api/0/{organization_slug}/{project_slug}/user-reports/\n533: API Keys\n534: Note\n535: API keys are a legacy means of authenticating. They will still be supported but are disabled for new accounts. You should use authentication tokens wherever possible.\n536: API keys are passed using HTTP Basic auth where the username is your api key, and the password is an empty value.\n537: As an example, to get information about the project which your key is bound to, you might make a request like so:\n538: Bash\n539: Copied\n540: curl -u {API_KEY}: https://sentry.io/api/0/organizations/{organization_slug}/projects/\n541: curl -u {API_KEY}: https://sentry.io/api/0/organizations/{organization_slug}/projects/\n542: You must pass a value for the password, which is the reason the : is present in our example.\n543: Previous\n544: API Reference\n545: Next\n546: Paginating Results\n547: Was this helpful?\n548: Yes 👍No 👎\n549: How can we improve this page?\n550: Email (optional)\n551: Submit feedback"
