      "numbered_text": "1: Sentry MCP\n2: Sentry MCP Server\n3: Connects AI assistants to Sentry for searching errors, analyzing performance, triaging issues, reading documentation, and managing projects — all via the Model Context Protocol.\n4: All connections use OAuth. The first connection will trigger an authentication flow to connect to your Sentry account.\n5: Connecting\n6: The base MCP server address is: https://mcp.sentry.dev/mcp\n7: You can optionally scope the connection to an organization or project:\n8: https://mcp.sentry.dev/mcp/{organizationSlug} — scoped to one organization\n9: https://mcp.sentry.dev/mcp/{organizationSlug}/{projectSlug} — scoped to one project\n10: When scoped, tools automatically default to the constrained org/project and unnecessary discovery tools are hidden. Scoping to a project is recommended when possible.\n11: Query Parameters\n12: ?experimental=1 — Enable forward-looking tool variants and experimental features\n13: Parameters can be combined: https://mcp.sentry.dev/mcp/my-org/my-project?experimental=1\n14: Setup Instructions\n15: Claude Code\n16: claude mcp add --transport http sentry https://mcp.sentry.dev/mcp/{organizationSlug}/{projectSlug}\n17: Cursor\n18: Use the \"Install MCP Server\" button, or manually add to MCP settings:\n19: {\n20: \"mcpServers\": {\n21: \"sentry\": {\n22: \"url\": \"https://mcp.sentry.dev/mcp/{organizationSlug}/{projectSlug}\"\n23: }\n24: }\n25: }\n26: VSCode\n27: Command Palette → \"MCP: Add Server\" → HTTP → enter the endpoint:\n28: https://mcp.sentry.dev/mcp/{organizationSlug}/{projectSlug}\n29: Other Clients\n30: Any MCP-compatible client can connect using the HTTP transport at the endpoint URL above.\n31: Local Server via the Sentry CLI\n32: Install the Sentry CLI and log in, then register sentry mcp as a stdio MCP server. It uses the CLI login, so the MCP config needs no token.\n33: curl https://cli.sentry.dev/install -fsS | bash\n34: sentry auth login\n35: claude mcp add sentry -- sentry mcp\n36: Other clients take the same command:\n37: {\n38: \"mcpServers\": {\n39: \"sentry\": {\n40: \"command\": \"sentry\",\n41: \"args\": [\"mcp\"]\n42: }\n43: }\n44: }\n45: The CLI also installs with brew install getsentry/tools/sentry, npm install -g sentry, or irm https://cli.sentry.dev/install.ps1 | iex on Windows. See https://cli.sentry.dev/getting-started/.\n46: Pass a target after the command to limit it:\n47: sentry mcp my-org/ — Limit to one organization\n48: sentry mcp my-org/my-project — Limit to a specific project\n49: For self-hosted Sentry, log in with sentry auth login --url https://sentry.example.com, then set SENTRY_HOST in the MCP server's environment. See https://cli.sentry.dev/self-hosted/.\n50: Run sentry mcp --help for every flag and environment variable. To run the server without installing the CLI, use the legacy npx @sentry/mcp-server package.\n51: llms.txt"
