        "observation": "quote: For `get_repository_tree`, `list_gists`, `get_gist`, `create_gist`, and `update_gist`, gist results retain file names, contents, sizes, language/type information, timestamps, visibility, and compact owner profiles, while omitting API/node and Git transport URLs. Tree entries omit their derivable API URLs. Create/update gist results contain the gist ID and HTML URL. Modern JSON text and structured content serialize the same compact result. Older or unknown protocol versions retain byte-for-byte legacy text without an output schema or structured content.",
